Item as amended agreed to.
Lace, including collars or collarettes of lace and all manufactures of lace;

Item agreed to.
(b) A tax of twenty iper cent on,-
Cigar and cigarette holders and pipes in excess of $2.50 each ;
Cigar and cigarette cases, ash trays and match boxes of gold or silver;
Humidors and smoking stands ;
Hunting and shooting garments and riding habits ;

Item agreed to.
A tax of fifteen per cent on,-
Boots, shoes, pumps and slippers of any material (not including shoes or appliances made to order for persons having a crippled or deformed foot or ankle, or to top boots not less than twelve inches in height such as are used in lumbering, mining and fishing industries, or to river driving boots fitted with caulks on soles thereof) in excess of $9 per pair;

This comes up in connection with the item of chandeliers which has already been -referred to and which was allowed to stand because changes were going to be made in it. I move:
That the words "Chandeliers except for churches" be struck out of paragraph (b) of resolution 1 and the following be inserted in resolution -3 :
Chandeliers, except for churches, in excess of $12 each;
Wall brackets, in excess of $3 each;
Gas and- electric light fixtures, not elsewhere specified, in excess of $3 each.
That covers the chandelier for the poor man's house, which -hon.. gentlemen were *speaking of at different times in the debate.
